WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.060
Speaker 1: All right.

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:07.629
Let's look at what it looks like when a nonreligious
person who is a Republican tries to pander

00:00:07.629 --> 00:00:08.910
to religious voters.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.320
It's actually quite depressing.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.190
Donald Trump appeared on the.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:14.700
I never fully understand what show.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:19.580
This is the flash point victory show.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:25.189
It's a religious Christian thing and it's
actually hilarious what happens.

00:00:25.189 --> 00:00:29.880
They one of the questions is framed about
how important Trump's faith is to him.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.430
And it's really funny because obviously it's
not true.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:35.490
Trump has never been religious, but he started
to pretend to be religious because he ran

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:36.829
as a Republican.

00:00:36.829 --> 00:00:38.059
This just gets like really awkward.

00:00:38.059 --> 00:00:40.379
And Trump spits out a word salad about religion.

00:00:40.379 --> 00:00:42.809
Speaker 3: Your faith is very important to
you.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:43.809
You've said that publicly.

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:44.809
Your faith is.

00:00:44.809 --> 00:00:45.809
Speaker 1: Important.

00:00:45.809 --> 00:00:46.809
Trump has said a lot of things that aren't
true.

00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:48.040
Speaker 3: But what does that mean to the
man?

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.980
Donald Trump Well, I think it means a lot
of things, but more to perhaps your listeners

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:55.629
and the people that will watch this show.

00:00:55.629 --> 00:00:58.780
And it's a very large group of people.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:04.470
For instance, I was the only president ever
go go to go to the big rally they had in Washington.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:05.470
Right.

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:06.530
Which they have on a yearly basis.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:08.570
Speaker 1: But I guess he means the March
for Life.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:14.869
Speaker 3: I guess the only one ever to go
as a president sitting president for life.

00:01:14.869 --> 00:01:16.850
And people were shocked.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:19.799
But even Ronald Reagan didn't want to take
that step.

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:23.049
And it was very close, always very close,
as you know, to the White House.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:25.570
It's almost like walking distance.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:27.550
But I went and I was proud of that.

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:31.010
I think we've been given credit for doing
that.

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:34.670
Speaker 1: But you can tell Trump is deeply
religious, deeply spiritual.

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:35.670
From this answer.

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:37.390
Speaker 3: People would say that was a courageous
thing to do.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:38.439
It was courageous.

00:01:38.439 --> 00:01:41.689
I viewed it as the right thing to do.

00:01:41.689 --> 00:01:49.860
But I was born into a family where my father
was religious, my mother was religious.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.170
I wouldn't say they were, you know, going
to church every single day.

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:55.250
They were you know, they were believers.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:58.659
Speaker 1: They were very privately religious,
such that no one knew it.

00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:01.620
Speaker 3: Even me and strong believers.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:06.960
I went to Sunday school, which was good and
which was expected.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.300
Like you, everybody goes to high school, right?

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:14.140
And when you think about it, the world is
so different now anyway.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:16.220
Speaker 1: So, you know, you get the gist.

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:21.720
They slammed Hillary Clinton for adopting
a sort of Southern drawl when she would speak

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.880
in front of some Southern crowds.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:29.129
In my mind, that's nothing compared to pretending
to be devoutly religious and against abortion

00:02:29.129 --> 00:02:34.060
when clearly you aren't and you haven't been
your entire life.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:38.780
TRUMP Of course there is no you never waste
the opportunity to claim that the left is

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:40.200
simply against religion.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.250
Speaker 3: They're against religion.

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:43.730
They're totally against religion.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.200
How do you get elected on these things?

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.879
They get elected by cheating, right?

00:02:47.879 --> 00:02:48.879
Speaker 1: Of course.

00:02:48.879 --> 00:02:55.200
The truth is what my listen, you can ask different
people on the left, you'll get different answers.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.890
I'm against religion playing a role in civil
government.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:07.530
I love freedom of religion, freedom to follow
any religious doctrine that speaks to you

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:15.239
or not to follow any and to have none of that
impact public policy nor how you were treated

00:03:15.239 --> 00:03:16.239
under the law.

00:03:16.239 --> 00:03:18.580
That's what I'm for as a member of the left.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:21.580
I'm not against religion.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:22.580
Trump then said.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:27.319
He's the only person who can stop Israel from
getting nuked by Iran, which is interesting.

00:03:27.319 --> 00:03:28.950
And there's a lot to say about this.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:33.400
Speaker 3: Under the Democrats, Israel will
be destroyed because Iran will have a nuclear

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.040
weapon and they will destroy Israel.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.860
They will use it too.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.840
So when you say fight a fight because we have
no choice.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:45.670
We have no choice and there's nobody else,
I don't believe that knows how to do this.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:46.830
Speaker 1: Right.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:53.280
So it's really important to understand that
the way in which Trump supporters are, quote,

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:58.810
pro-Israel is a very specific thing from the
evangelical Christian community.

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:00.349
The viewers of this show.

00:04:00.349 --> 00:04:06.930
Okay, The viewers of this show support Israel
not because of any concern about antisemitism

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:12.599
or Jews or it's because they believe that
supporting Israel will precipitate the second

00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:18.829
coming of Christ, after which most or all
of the Jews die, depending on which belief

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:21.360
system you adhere to.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.780
That's why they are, quote, supporters of
Israel.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.540
And that's what Trump is paying lip service
to.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:30.000
And then lastly, Trump saying the Johnson
amendment is a terrible thing.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.820
If you don't know what that is, I'll tell
you in a moment.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:37.320
Speaker 3: I'm asking, why don't you use your
power so that you can be treated better?

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:41.450
And then one person said, well, we have the
Johnson Amendment, which basically would take

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:46.830
our tax exemption and our tax basis away from
us, which is unbelievably severe.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:50.000
We put put you out of business.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:57.331
I said so that actually the people and I was
at the top of Trump Tower way up high, and

00:04:57.331 --> 00:04:59.470
I looked down at the sidewalk and you see
all the people.

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:04.590
I said, So anybody off the street, then you're
saying has more power than the people in this

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:05.590
room?

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:06.590
Because.

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:07.919
Speaker 1: Okay, so let me explain to you
what Trump is saying here.

00:05:07.919 --> 00:05:13.310
The Johnson Amendment is a tax code provision
from 1954.

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:20.840
When we say nonprofit churches aren't allowed
to do politics or they jeopardize their tax

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:22.300
exempt status.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.100
What we're talking about partially comes from
the Johnson Amendment.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:29.669
The Johnson Amendment said if you're a five,
a1c3 nonprofit organization, you can't endorser

00:05:29.669 --> 00:05:30.850
oppose political candidates.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:36.620
And of course, as we know, dozens and dozens,
hundreds, thousands of churches, particularly

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:44.080
evangelical churches and other forms of Christianity,
Protestantism regularly do politics and often

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:46.350
overtly endorse or oppose candidates.

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:49.440
They should lose their tax exempt status.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:54.250
Trump is saying, No, it's too harsh because
then it actually makes them impotent in some

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:56.300
way relative to random people.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:59.820
Well, the whole point is we will give you
something special, something privileged under

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:02.560
the tax code, which is nonprofit status.

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:07.669
But you can't engage in politics because that's
a way to circumvent all of the campaign finance

00:06:07.669 --> 00:06:10.160
infrastructure that is there for a particular
reason.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:13.030
So Trump doesn't like that Trump wants to
get rid of that.

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:19.970
This is the height or the bottom of the barrel,
depending on your view of pandering to a group

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:22.830
of voters that, yes, Trump does need.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:07:08.970
He rightly assesses that he needs them in
the most pathetic 

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:41.320
way possible.

